{"type":"text","text":"Done — mapping sheet 3 complete for **Super Mario Bros. (World)**, scene World 1-1. All work was done blind (no reference), by differential search plus one disassembly read, and every claim was proven by a write and a screenshot.\n\n## Results\n\n| Value | Address | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| World number | **`$075F`** | binary, 0-based — displayed world = value + 1 (1-1 holds 0) |\n| Level number | **`$075C`** | binary, 0-based — displayed level = value + 1 (1-1 holds 0) |\n| Mario horizontal position | **`$0086`** | binary 0–255, level x mod 256 |\n| Mario vertical position | **`$00CE`** | binary, screen y of sprite top (down = larger; 176 on the ground in 1-1) |\n\nSupporting addresses found along the way: **`$071C`** = screen scroll x (level's left edge, mod 256), **`$03AD`** = derived Mario on-screen x = `$0086` − `$071C` (a copy, rewritten every frame).\n\n## How each was found and proven\n\n**Horizontal `$0086`** — Two `diff_memory` rounds on \"hold Right\" narrowed 167 → 41 survivors; `$0005`, `$03AD`, `$0755` and `$0086` all tracked screen x. `trace_writes` on the copy `$03AD` gave writer PC `$F17F`, whose hand-decoded code is `LDA $86,X / SEC / SBC $071C / STA $03AD,Y` — so `$03AD = $0086 − $071C` and `$0086` is the master. Writing `$03AD = 200` did nothing (snapped back to 40 on the next frame), while **`write_memory $0086 = 200`** moved Mario from screen x≈40 to **x≈200** — the screenshot showed him standing at the right-hand bush instead of the start hill. Note on the \"page byte\" hint: it exists only as a mod‑256 coordinate. A watched run showed `$0086` wrap 251→9 while the screen scrolled, and no separate player page byte turned up in `$0718–$0727`; the level page is carried by the scroll `$071C` and the nametable, not by a player page cell.\n\n**Vertical `$00CE`** — Holding A for 10 frames and diffing `decreased` gave `$00CE` 176 → 141 (copies `$03B8` and OAM y `$0204/$0208` moved identically). **`write_memory $00CE = 120`** then left Mario hanging in the sky — the screenshot shows him floating above the bushes rather than standing on the ground.\n\n**World and level** — They never change by playing, so I used the `$0750` block and wrote distinctive test values. In 1-1 `$075F` and `$075C` both read 0. I wrote **`$075F = 4`** and **`$075C = 2`**, then held Right ~300 frames to die. The death screenshot shows the fixed HUD *and* the black card reading **`WORLD 5-3`** (5 = 4+1, 3 = 2+1). Because the two distinct values landed in separate digit positions, the world/level assignment is unambiguous.\n\n## Recorded\nSix `record_mapping` entries (the four above plus `$071C` and `$03AD`), all `confidence: 1`, `source: \"differential search\"`, each with encoding and proof in the notes. `promote_mappings` saved 6 discoveries to `mappings/sha1-33d23c2f…json` (0 hypotheses skipped). The emulator was restored from save state to a clean World 1-1 and left running."}
